  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Calculate $F(2)$ where $F(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$F(2)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Evaluating $F(x)$ at $x=2,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\nF(2)={\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nNow, computing the definite integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{t}^{3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{4}-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
